<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Filippo Maria Visconti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1392–1447</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Filippo Maria Visconti (1392–1447) was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1412, the last of the Visconti line. He rebuilt the state of his father, Gian Galeazzo, after its collapse and waged long wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a>, relying on condottieri such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francesco-sforza">Francesco Sforza</a>, to whom he married his only child, the illegitimate Bianca Maria. After his death without a legitimate heir, Milan briefly became the Golden Ambrosian Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/filippo-maria-visconti.jpg" alt="Filippo Maria Visconti" width="320" height="498" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pisanello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisanello_-_Codex_Vallardi_2484.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
